    "created_at": "2016-12-09T15:29:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-09T15:30:56Z",
    "body": " I don't think there is an issue with the spec, at least as far as ambiguity is concerned.\r\ntl;dr: the canvas shall be cleared if it has a 2d context, but not if it has a webgl context.\r\n\r\nThe spec text for this is right here: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#attr-canvas-width\r\nThe text is explicit about the fact that the steps for [setting bitmap dimensions](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#concept-canvas-set-bitmap-dimensions) must be followed in the case where width or height are \"redundantly set to the value they already have\" on a canvas that has a 2D context.\r\n\r\nFor WebGL however the spec is different. It says: \"The table below also shows the value to which these buffers shall be cleared when first created, when the size is changed, or after presentation when the preserveDrawingBuffer context creation attribute is false.\"\r\nReference: https://www.khronos.org/registry/webgl/specs/latest/1.0/#2.2\r\n\r\nChrome does this AFAIK, we test this behavior. There must be something particular about that use case that is triggering a bug in Chrome.  I will follow-up on this in the Chromium issue tracker.\r\n\r\n@smfr: Do you have repro steps for observing the issue on http://tesseract.projectnaptha.com? I looked at the summaries of the project's [issues](https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js/issues) and I did not see any open issues related to this.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
