    "created_at": "2016-12-09T16:31:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-09T16:31:21Z",
    "body": "Looking at the code for the website, in particular this file : http://tesseract.projectnaptha.com/animation/animate.js\r\n\r\nWhat I notice is that the scroll event listener resizes the canvas without redrawing the canvas contents (which leaves the canvas blank).  This however should not cause any flickering because there is a requestAnimationFrame loop in progress and animation callbacks are guaranteed to be the last things to run before a rendering context graphics update,  as specified in the event loop processing model:\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model\r\n(see step 7.10)\r\n\r\nMy best guess would be that perhaps there is a user agent intervention interfering with the page. Is it possible that Safari and Firefox are attempting to pause animations while the page is scrolling or something like that?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
