    "created_at": "2016-12-09T16:34:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-09T16:34:04Z",
    "body": "I think the real explanation is that Safari and Firefox are firing scroll events asynchronously, so the timing of those and rAF are different vs. Chrome. We've seen this on other sites too (e.g. flickery headers when scrolling twitter).\r\n\r\nThanks for the diagnosis. I'll close this.",
